      "side": 1,
      "message": "Assuming the shader snippet\u0027s definition is valid, when this-\u003eneedsLocalCoords() is false, it shouldn\u0027t every reference the coords parameter.\n\nI tried to look at what the default code gen does, and it looks like its functions skip the `float2 pos` parameter when needsLocalCoords() is false, so it shouldn\u0027t matter what we pass in under those circumstances. \n\nCan we get away with just passing in `\"localCoordsVar\"` in the call to `emit_glue_code_for_entry()`? If not, and we need to call functions that still have a float2 parameter that\u0027s internally ignored, we can pass in a constant expression like `float2(0)` so we don\u0027t have to define other variables.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 157,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 158,
        "endChar": 88
      },
      "revId": "e9aa0ff77cfa01190b1f2f8dc80b23754b570c4d",
